 HISTORY                                                          3053 1451
 -------                                                          3053 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  3053 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The        3053 1451
 inelastic thermal scattering law data for Al2O3 (sapphire) was   3053 1451
 developed using the ab-initio lattice dynamics methods [1]. The  3053 1451
 Full Law Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to generate     3053 1451
 MF=7 data for O in Al2O3 with mass and free atom cross sections  3053 1451
 as shown below [2]. Sapphire is typically used as a single       3053 1451
 crystal neutron filter, whereby elastic scattering is            3053 1451
 negligible [3]. This library, therefore, contains only           3053 1451
 inelastic scattering data (MT = 4).                              3053 1451
                                                                  3053 1451
